# Slack Modal Trigger Safety

Slack `trigger_id` values expire in a few seconds. Handlers that open modals must
call `views.open` before awaited Ray/DB/Redis/Slack I/O.

## Standard pattern (RAY-72999)

Use the helpers in `app/slack/modal_trigger.py`:

1. `ack()`
2. `view_id = await open_loading_modal(client, body["trigger_id"])`
3. `await populate_ray_connection(context)` (do **not** use `middleware=[ray_connection]` on these handlers — that I/O runs before the listener)
4. slow work (`require_ray_client`, pricing, settings, …)
5. `await safe_views_update(client, view_id, final_or_error_view)`

`status_modal(...)` / `request_error_modal()` cover login/error outcomes after the
loading modal is already open.

## Avoid before `views_open(...)`

- `client.files_info(...)` / `get_accessible_slack_files(...)` / `download_file(...)`
- Ray, Verify, or LanguageCloud API calls
- Redis/database/settings lookups
- `middleware=[ray_connection]` on the modal-open action itself

Keep deleted/inaccessible Slack file checks in submit/download paths, not
modal-open triggers.

When reviewing modal-trigger changes, audit every `await` between `ack()` and
`views_open(...)`.
